 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<opaque>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: a page of items ordered by
+  ascending `id`. `limit` defaults to 20. Omit `cursor` for the first page and
+  pass each `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page; the final page
+  returns `"next_cursor": null`. An invalid limit or cursor returns status
+  400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
